[38;2;124;124;124mCharacteristic of an integral domain is the smallest positive n such that n·1 = [0m[38;2;124;124;124m0, or 0 if no such n exists. For integral domains, characteristic is either 0 or[0m[38;2;124;124;124ma prime.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mKey: A ⊆ B as rings (subring). The identity 1_A is the identity of A. Is 1_A = [0m
