[38;2;124;124;124mby the kernel of the map ℤ → R, n ↦ n·1. Since A → B is injective ring [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mhomomorphism, the kernel of ℤ → A equals kernel of ℤ → B (because n·1_A maps to [0m[38;2;124;124;124mn·1_B, and n·1_A = 0 iff its image n·1_B = 0 by injectivity). So char A = char [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mB.[0m

